Conclusions

- The structure was of very poor quality, and my lack of planning made everything even worse.
For my next project, the ideal would be to prepare earlier, and choose more professional material
options, instead of legoes and hotwheels tracks.

- CAD modeling is a great tool to learn, I underestimated the difficulty of assembling the system.

- It was a great idea to buy metal gear servos, they are gonna be useful even for later projects.

- The PID system is very cool to tweak, but it would be better to have a better done project so that the
poor structure wouldnt influence on the feedback loop.
